Distinguish isolation, dependency resolution, pins, and available artifacts (@rc-locking: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @reproducible-computation, #source "../sources/Python-Environments-and-Packaging.lingua#r_5VVAF04TH8R3DRY9Z36308BH88", #source "../sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ", #reproducible-computation "System-libraries-and-hardware.lingua#r_6MEK7DSTADH24AV1NAQBG5SR61") { r_5BEV7Q4J6K3CGCFRHANDW6JXRY
**Read:** [Environments, dependency records, and packaging — PyPA](../sources/Python-Environments-and-Packaging.lingua#r_5VVAF04TH8R3DRY9Z36308BH88), all dependency/environment tutorials and the relevant lock-file specification; [The Turing Way — reproducible research, collaboration, and preservation](../sources/The-Turing-Way.lingua#r_5K6W3KETGFH4N3SDYCB5V0Q3MZ), Capturing Computational Environments and environment-management material.

An isolated environment separates installed packages from another environment. Dependency resolution selects versions and artifacts satisfying constraints for a platform. A pin fixes a chosen version or identity. A lock records a resolved choice under a tool's contract. None of these terms alone says that every required artifact is still obtainable or that rebuilding it yields the same behavior.

Inspect direct and transitive dependencies, interpreter constraints, optional extras, platform markers, source locations, artifact hashes, and resolver/tool versions. A list of top-level package names is weaker than a complete resolved environment. Conversely, a platform-specific wheel collection may reconstruct one target well while saying little about another operating system or architecture.

Use the official packaging tutorials and the current specifications supported by your selected tool. Do not assume a filename convention makes a file a portable lock, or that every tool supports every current specification. Preserve the declaration, resolved information, and reconstruction command, then test a new environment rather than modifying an old one until it happens to work.

**Work:** reconstruct the worked standard-library program under an explicitly selected interpreter. For a second project using NumPy, distinguish declared requirements from the resolved artifacts actually installed. Change the interpreter or platform in a disposable environment and explain how resolution differs. Identify which necessary inputs would be unavailable during an offline reconstruction.

The report should state the environment claim's boundary: one identified environment, a tested family of environments, or a bounded numerical result across them. Availability, isolation, deterministic artifact identity, and scientific validity remain separate findings. Later container and declarative-environment readings supply two concrete approaches for broader system dependencies.

**Continue:** [Native libraries, operating systems, and hardware can change a computation](System-libraries-and-hardware.lingua#r_6MEK7DSTADH24AV1NAQBG5SR61).

